      "side": 1,
      "message": "Even with this `cflush()` on each iteration, I find that if the output contains hundreds of lines, then it will get truncated, that is, after a while, the test of the  output (including the next command prompt character `\"\u003e \"`) will not make it out of the USB stream.  Because of this, I have currently limited the number of lines that will be printed by a single command invocation to 32, forcing opentitantool to repeatedly request more, sidestepping the issue.\n\nI would rather understand what guarantees `cflush()` provides, and how I can achieve printing an unbounded number of lines.  Do anyone have suggestion for this?",
      "revId": "5827f8e4e94baadb0c856696b84383a520d70f9e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
